      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's true that nothing can \"fix\" a life that feels this broken, and that permanence is a heavy thing to carry. Instead of trying to fix the past, maybe you could focus on just making the next moment a little less painful. A good therapist won't magically erase your mistakes, but they can give you tools to manage the crushing weight of what you feel. Even a small shift in perspective can make a difference when everything feels like a dead end.",
      "source": "target",
